    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210-a3">

                <pb facs="1263" n="1105" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1105"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Thompson to the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-01-08"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Permit me to thank your excellency
                    for your kind note of the 3d instant, with which you have been pleased to
                    accompany copy of a communication from the attorney-general of Mexico advising
                    you that the delivery of the American fishing vessels captured off the coast of
                    Campeche will soon be made, under bond, in accordance with the decision
                    pronounced to that end by the judge who has the case in hand.</p>
                <p>Renewing to you my deep appreciation for your excellency’s good offices in this
                    matter, it affords me pleasure to assure you of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. E. Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
